    "final_answer": "Final Answer:\n- Report: outputs/reports/knockout_inference_summary.md\n- Key Results:\n  - The expression data separate into two clear groups: KO_1/KO_2 (experimental) vs Control_1/Control_2/Control_3 (controls).\n  - One gene shows a uniquely strong on/off pattern: it is robustly expressed in all control samples and completely absent in both KO samples, with an extremely large negative log2 fold-change.\n  - Using the gene identifiers provided in the dataset, the inferred knocked-out gene is:\n    \n    **Gene symbol (as represented in the data): `100126348`**\n\n- Artifacts:\n  - Dataset overview: outputs/reports/dataset_overview.md\n  - Knockout gene rationale: outputs/reports/knockout_gene_selection.md\n  - Sample groups: outputs/tables/sample_group_assignments.tsv\n  - Per-gene group statistics: outputs/tables/differential_expression_results.tsv\n  - Ranked knockout-like candidates: outputs/tables/knockout_candidate_genes_ranked.tsv\n  - Final knockout call: outputs/tables/final_knockout_gene.tsv\n  - Summary report: outputs/reports/knockout_inference_summary.md\n- Figures:\n  ![Sample clustering (controls vs KO)](outputs/figures/sample_clustering_embedding.png)\n- Caveats & Warnings:\n  - The only gene identifier available in the expression matrices is a numeric `GeneID`; no symbol column is present, and the provided compressed `gene_info.gz` could not be read with the available tools. Thus, `100126348` is reported directly as the gene “symbol” in the sense of being the unique gene identifier in this dataset.\n- Next Steps:\n  - If an official HGNC/NCBI/Ensembl gene symbol is required, map GeneID `100126348` to its symbol using an external annotation resource.",
